WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.300
[Music]

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.580
[Narrarator:] Today, these men, soldiers of a free country, are leaving to fight.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.330
Today our battlefield is the world.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:37.400
Our transports, our freighters, go to the furthest islands of the earth.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.020
Men of the United Nations are landing everywhere.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:52.630
Soldiers from New York and Chicago are moving up to fight in the empty desert.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.610
To fight on battlefields of snow.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:06.310
And in the jungle, men from the little towns of Montana, moving up in the heat of Asia, Africa, the Caribbean.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.130
Their job is fighting.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:16.030
They must be kept safe -- against disease, against the special dangers of the jungle.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.400
Behind all men stand scientists of the western hemisphere.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:28.270
These doctors are good neighbors from two American countries: United States and the Republic of Colombia.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.980
Here were their first battles.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.990
Their weapons: the test tube, the sterilized needle.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:38.740
Between the equator and the Panama Canal they fought their silent war.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.390
Their enemy was hidden in the green branches of the jungle.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:48.030
Here the heat of the sky pours down 12 hours a day.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:54.170
There is no autumn, no spring, only months of heat and months of rain.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:02:00.590
Life is quick and abundant, and death is also abundant.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.840
Here was the home of jungle yellow fever.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:11.310
A man who came here to work, or to fight, on these dark trails was condemned to grow sick, delirious.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.600
Eyes and skin turning yellow before he died.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:21.240
A disease of young men, of those who built a house or camp in the infected forest.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.820
Death waited for them in the heat of the valley.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:31.110
Wooden crosses for the young men who dared to walk in the jungle.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.700
They died from the bite of a mosquito.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.560
In a few laboratories they put this disease behind glass and studied it.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:46.620
It was a virus, it had to be fed on living tissue, on unborn chicks, and human blood serum.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.140
It was dangerous and invisible. Had killed men who had worked with it.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:07.200
What they needed was a vaccine to prevent yellow fever and the fight never stopped 'til it was found.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:13.770
'Til it was tested, purified. 'Til it could be dried and frozen and prepared in quantities.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.710
Until it could be transported.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:23.280
The first battle had been won inside the white walls of a laboratory.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.240
The second battle was here, in the heat and wet of the jungle.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.020
Above their heads was the solution to the mystery of jungle yellow fever.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:41.630
The guilty mosquitoes lived and bred not in pools on the ground, but in the treetops.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.380
They bit not only men, but animals - especially monkeys.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:50.020
And thousands of monkeys grew sick but did not die.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.630
Their blood was a living reservoir of yellow fever.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:04:01.840
Mosquitoes which had fed on these monkeys, flew down from the treetops, attacked men, and infected them with a virus of yellow fever.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.300
The ride on these trails became a sentence of death.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:16.590
But carried in this thermos jug, too precious to go on mule-back, are tubes of vaccine packed in ice.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:19.750
Moving over narrow trails and slippery bridges.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:26.970
In a jungle area without railroads, without highways. Across rivers too steep for navigation.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:31.950
At night they set up their portable refrigerator unit to renew the supply of ice.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:37.060
In the morning, it is carried on mule back with the needles and syringes.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.370
A task force against yellow fever.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:53.420
It's a grey hot Sunday in the town of Copair [?]. It's market day, too, and there is good news.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:01.170
Yes, it is true. The doctors are coming.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.530
[Bell tower rings]

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:08.810
Sunday mass is just over and in front of the church the news spreads.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.690
It is true, it is printed.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:16.510
It is signed by the mayor. The priest himself has given his blessing.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.480
It has come at last.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:30.050
Now, the slow pack-train climbs up the hill from the jungle.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.690
The doctors have come to the town of Copair.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:55.020
Fiebre amarilla. The yellow fever. The fever that eats men, that kills their father,their brothers.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.950
The fever of the jungle is to be feared no longer.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:02.420
The blessed medicine has come.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:12.590
Years of difficult work, years of collaboration between men of the United States, Cuba, Panama, Brazil, Colombia.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:20.130
Years of courage in the laboratory and in the jungle come to their climax here, in this patio of the mayor's house.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:23.540
The vaccination will be here in the open air.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:30.010
It is a dull, cloudy afternoon, two hundred miles north of the equator.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:38.230
The vaccine is removed from the thermos jug.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:41.860
The instruments are sterilized in boiling water.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:50.960
There are people here who read slowly, others who have never learned, but there's one word they know: vacunacion.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:56.610
Vaccination. That word means life.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:05.010
And they know one thing more -- that if three are sick with yellow fever, two will surely die and only one will live.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.940
The names of the people are written down.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.620
The harness-maker's wife; a farmer; his son.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:28.950
A woman is the first to be vaccinated and now two more.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:47.250
These are a mixed people, descendents of Indians and of the Spanish conquerors.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:10.980
A few drops of vaccine injected under the skin of the arm will give them dependable and lasting immunity.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:17.090
Those whose names are in this book need have no fear of yellow fever.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:20.860
And there's only one shot and there is no illness afterwards.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:24.830
The protection lasts for years, perhaps for life.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:28.410
It is a product of the genius of the combined Americans.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:32.930
Already five hundred thousand citizens of Colombia have been vaccinated.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:55.560
Now the vaccine is taken to army hospitals where the entire Colombian army, unit-by-unit, is vaccinated against yellow fever.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.340
Now they can go safely to their outposts in the jungle.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:16.530
These soldiers are safe and because of this pioneering work, when our heavy guns are lifted in the jungle, the men behind them will be strong.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:24.220
Ready to fight in the African Congo, on the dark islands of the South Pacific, in the jungles of Burma, in the Solomon's,

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:31.690
in the depths of New Guinea, in the Philippines when we've come to take them one-by-one.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.460
Our men, today, are safe against yellow fever.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.430
Free to fight the worst disease of all: fascism.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:49.380
Until that too, shall be blasted from the face of the earth.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:10:00.030
[The End]

